#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192794 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192518 :question/id #uuid "6f7bdbcf-fb8e-5c70-b368-4e73cc94bdb2" :question/math-academy-id "e-11112" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{4x-y}{x+y^2},$ evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{4x-y}{x+{y}^{2}}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x-y)\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2})}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot 1}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4x+4{y}^{2}-4x+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{2}+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(2,-1)} & =\\frac{4(-1)^{2}+(-1)}{{(2+{(-1)}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c6e3db-073b-5867-8137-1d8660b20887" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048842 :topic/difficulty 1.2766246463083966 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428105 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-