wer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{π^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190986} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d5d22f-128f-5fc9-a4ce-b6d714c1614e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190984}] :question/id #uuid "735de4aa-bbaf-5aea-a3dc-f11c48509e1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-158466" :question/problem "For the function $f(x, y) = \\frac{\\cos x}{x + y}$, evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(π, 0)$." :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule while holding $y$ fixed,\n$$\nf_x(x,y)=\\frac{-(x+y)\\sin x-\\cos x}{(x+y)^2}.\n$$\nAt $(\\pi,0)$, the denominator is nonzero and\n$$\nf_x(\\pi,0)=\\frac{-\\pi\\sin\\pi-\\cos\\pi}{\\pi^2}=\\frac1{\\pi^2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa77c537-04b8-5f36-ad44-5700f53a5a37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4xy + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191027} {:answer/id #uuid "b229ff52-79c1-591c-a0e0-e0f957d9821a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2}y^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191028} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb7ab21-162d-5ec1-b6e8-26edb0489e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy^{2} + 4x + y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191029} {:answer/id #uuid "cf89793f-3b35-5f96-819f-5dc8bec86e1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy^{2} - 4x^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191030} {:answer/id #uuid "68887cfb-914c-5dca-a509-4e7ad277cfc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2}y - 4y^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68887cfb-914c-5dca-a509-4e7ad277cfc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2}y - 4y^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191031} :answer-field/id #uuid "03210637-c25d-5dce-8f00-d4c6e3ceca85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191026}] :question/id #uuid "4223a1e7-2b20-5d20-9827-89ebd1b2b448" :question/math-academy-id "q-159724" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x, y) = \\frac{e^{y^{2}}}{x^{2} - 2y}$. The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n$\\frac{∂f}{∂y} = (h(x, y)e^{y^{2}})/((x^{2} - 2y)^{2})$.\nFind the function $h(x, y)$." :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule gives\n$$\nf_y=\\frac{(2ye^{y^2})(x^2-2y)-e^{y^2}(-2)}{(x^2-2y)^2}\n=\\frac{(2x^2y-4y^2+2)e^{y^2}}{(x^2-2y)^2}.\n$$\nThus $h(x,y)=2x^2y-4y^2+2$. The derivative is defined where $x^2-2y\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "124ba60a-ec47-5dd9-97fc-d33ccf7d0e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275645} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa03d48-f644-5066-b304-d3fc3f4f62eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276292} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6c70be-1878-50b5-989f-a8ed0e5f587f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276303} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b747a7-3b88-5c3b-b25b-53403f09d052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276925} {:answer/id #uuid "ec320ce3-f38d-5b16-8a80-a7b57185a46a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "124ba60a-ec47-5dd9-97fc-d33ccf7d0e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275645} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4deb5e-7cf6-55ae-b93a-f09121cdee49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95a36042-f58f-5fde-b6a7-7ca45f1d6809" :question/math-academy-id "q-159700" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}{\\operatorname{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{\\operatorname{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{\\operatorname{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,\\pi /2)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-(\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-0}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8543754a-baf7-532f-9aaa-3f6e2f377989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276670} {:answer/id #uuid "872098d7-2da8-563d-9dbe-aa0ef1581439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276693} {:answer/id #uuid "9f76ba1c-fbca-5e67-ba0f-95af73b7592a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276912} {:answer/id #uuid "f00a4060-bf7f-5ccd-83cc-feaade45b7ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277585} {:answer/id #uuid "f0139e5c-4ac7-5bda-a049-12fd07049209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f00a4060-bf7f-5ccd-83cc-feaade45b7ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277585} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b4f281e-3538-5167-b8db-a9dda1fcb94e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277972}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c6d2d99-f435-50ff-85c3-a966d3aa1af6" :question/math-academy-id "q-159709" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(0,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(0,2)} & =\\frac{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-0\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+0}{(2+0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a420460-c7c1-505e-8ad4-c9bb108a6ff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275860} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9d3b68-4176-5fa0-9407-0ed4c3eb41a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276332} {:answer/id #uuid "883a161b-2779-571d-bfa4-409b6a959feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276708} {:answer/id #uuid "b96f1c91-267d-539d-9fa8-52a5e328fc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277120} {:answer/id #uuid "dfef293c-ea14-5c29-b5c4-17120a6c650d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96f1c91-267d-539d-9fa8-52a5e328fc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277120} :answer-field/id #uuid "af4b38e9-c4a5-5254-be14-837fef119079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c75dffc7-c60f-5338-92f4-7c0c6ff2bb72" :question/math-academy-id "q-159713" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x+y)\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x+y})}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y))}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot 1)}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{6(x+y)-(3x+y)}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\right)}{x+y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x+5y}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=3x+5y.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1071740e-9558-5e73-b52c-d383864bf497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275622} {:answer/id #uuid "9e058e90-be98-5313-a164-e37b5eaec24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276896} {:answer/id #uuid "b028380b-a597-535a-bd93-8b4c6734b700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277053} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6cb830-da03-564b-9a88-50ef70b7374f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+{x}^{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277142} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d0d589-d5cc-550b-974e-b4afdfaebb22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e058e90-be98-5313-a164-e37b5eaec24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276896} :answer-field/id #uuid "75024153-b4e7-530d-be37-6a2d7adf8ab7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277934}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad571fe8-149e-54b6-a89f-66ae79db7481" :question/math-academy-id "q-159714" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{2h(x,y)}{{x}^{3}y}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot 2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{3}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=1-x{y}^{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e44334-00de-5702-83e5-16a7570d043c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2x+y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276427} {:answer/id #uuid "8aac973e-8257-545d-b095-ab149936e003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276733} {:answer/id #uuid "b7cf2fa9-6053-5c4d-852e-474c37939e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277108} {:answer/id #uuid "dd338f07-9cf2-51fd-a11c-32c271645616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277414} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b315c7-d154-5db9-8a29-731dc66826e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd338f07-9cf2-51fd-a11c-32c271645616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277414} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c3c66f0-c7ef-59da-9462-dd34d39d1caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "485c686b-8a53-5bf0-8bc4-72a915a1ba56" :question/math-academy-id "q-159723" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{y}^{2})}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (-2y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{y}^{3}+2{x}^{2}y+2{y}^{3}}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy+2{x}^{2}y}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1+x)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=2xy(1+x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "764fe799-f9d4-56fc-8786-768351e90b2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381260} {:answer/id #uuid "af40a1cc-fcdd-5d82-88f1-afb1cb810dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381261} {:answer/id #uuid "238d2bb5-2057-5938-92cb-490c8fd1d052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381262} {:answer/id #uuid "007df772-538e-5628-b388-eb1493c3de4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381263} {:answer/id #uuid "e31f346f-c25e-5e5e-9897-5f3acda1e293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af40a1cc-fcdd-5d82-88f1-afb1cb810dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381261} :answer-field/id #uuid "33cf4f0d-d3ae-5f4a-af95-43db53f9c0fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381259}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba29a24e-25aa-5034-8849-e753260af75f" :question/math-academy-id "q-159706" :question/problem "For the function $$\n\\displaystyle f(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y},\n$$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(\\pi ,-\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,-\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,-\\pi )} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(-1)(-1)}{(-1-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8367eed8-8db9-5b16-8030-4fb1d45343f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381267} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f7d926-4b2e-5a47-a964-89bbf3409d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{e}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381268} {:answer/id #uuid "c0684d01-ce2e-5d72-b7c5-5083711bc071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381269} {:answer/id #uuid "3e29fb6f-8142-5709-a889-a0d7208a0ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381270} {:answer/id #uuid "20723cc1-5581-5f10-b006-0cc5888b60c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8367eed8-8db9-5b16-8030-4fb1d45343f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381267} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43d33af-7b21-5589-9d8f-5fccd66d3600" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381266}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6f6e1b67-30d1-5d26-980f-cea342aa0dc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-159707" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{e}^{y-x}},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{e}^{y-x}}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{y-x}-({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y-x})}{{({e}^{y-x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\cdot {e}^{y-x}-({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{y-x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-x)}{{({e}^{y-x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x{e}^{y-x}-({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{y-x}\\cdot (-1)}{{({e}^{y-x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}){e}^{y-x}}{{({e}^{y-x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{e}^{y-x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1,-1)} & =\\frac{2(1)+{1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}}{{e}^{-1-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+1-1}{{e}^{-2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b4a1d9-cd1c-5571-9518-79d29836ff46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381274} {:answer/id #uuid "12f38844-8972-566b-9cc4-9cfde5403c8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381275} {:answer/id #uuid "c7c9d0a7-3b5f-5c87-8d2d-3652e6d79b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381276} {:answer/id #uuid "83292db4-d816-5e9e-a3de-33ff1b3276fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381277} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8d819d-5775-5389-a036-8dc2fb90c6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83292db4-d816-5e9e-a3de-33ff1b3276fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381277} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cc5a44e-5e88-5654-addf-13837aea580f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381273}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9fb48fb-ee18-53c2-9d40-be28dc7c4677" :question/math-academy-id "q-159722" :question/problem "Consider the function $$\n\\displaystyle f(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}.\n$$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dde26e5-909a-5520-b5a4-d567f4f30d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436556} {:answer/id #uuid "8e6e21a7-d420-5add-b68c-d19db196b561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436559} {:answer/id #uuid "ab23a96c-3799-57cf-a6c2-1ae6ae0bc1c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436568} {:answer/id #uuid "c12523e2-dee4-5166-961f-0a9b274f76d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436573} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a4e0d8-9189-5dce-8c93-80f07feaa44f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dde26e5-909a-5520-b5a4-d567f4f30d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436556} :answer-field/id #uuid "1990b86b-b897-5e01-b1d1-8c99349fdebe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436593}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26e723d1-2e7d-5b20-b4fd-e3325c571238" :question/math-academy-id "q-159696" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{3xy-1}{2x-3y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{3xy-1}{2x-3y}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3xy-1)\\cdot (2x-3y)-(3xy-1)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x-3y)}{(2x-3y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x\\cdot (2x-3y)-(3xy-1)\\cdot (-3)}{(2x-3y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}-9xy+9xy-3}{(2x-3y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}-3}{(2x-3y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(0,-1)} & =\\frac{6(0)^{2}-3}{(2(0)-3(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eb1fcd4-1769-591e-b2b3-2926ae221a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{y}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436539} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5aa69d-a57a-53e7-a411-7b8d1e231bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436542} {:answer/id #uuid "8397e509-d007-5ca5-ab7f-b6777f6c8813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436551} {:answer/id #uuid "898b4cbe-f73a-573e-8210-8119141fd3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436553} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f7930b-c4f8-5a1e-9abf-4982ea59ffa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8397e509-d007-5ca5-ab7f-b6777f6c8813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436551} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6e9e9d-4e43-54d1-b414-a2a8e2b2fbf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436602}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27e4d0e6-6215-57d4-b123-69cd51f3932f" :question/math-academy-id "q-159720" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{xy}}{xy}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y){e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}y}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{{e}^{xy}}{xy}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})\\cdot xy-{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)}{(xy)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)\\cdot xy-{e}^{xy}\\cdot y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{xy}\\cdot y\\cdot xy-y{e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y{e}^{xy}(xy-1)}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(xy-1){e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=xy-1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49517556-0d0e-548e-a3c1-8430dc1612ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436543} {:answer/id #uuid "92355996-2538-5d06-adbb-60fbc547dfd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436560} {:answer/id #uuid "d25dbf87-9ff4-5222-983d-a08125cb25b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436578} {:answer/id #uuid "d9cd43b3-1131-5c70-bf1e-5c97871cb3df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436579} {:answer/id #uuid "f122d57b-621e-5f14-a573-0116c8efb68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d25dbf87-9ff4-5222-983d-a08125cb25b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436578} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b91fb5a-fb60-5758-b55c-b8f8d909486c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436596}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f311e12c-1089-5d71-97f6-83e1fd9c3339" :question/math-academy-id "q-159702" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{y}},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{y}}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y})}{{(\\sqrt{y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2y\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{4{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\right)}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}}{2y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(3,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(3,1)} & =\\frac{{3}^{2}+3(1)^{2}}{2(1)\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9+3}{2} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436614 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cc88c0d-b906-5169-8020-771089d1d342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436541} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8f703d-08c4-5364-a106-a8206935b823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-11y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436547} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2c81c3-bd1b-576f-8ea5-5e15ecc6a989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-22y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436558} {:answer/id #uuid "9aa74480-20e7-5b9c-bfdf-57f701ad6150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11y-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436561} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bd98b7-39d1-5926-929c-4305a2b89c9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+11y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aa74480-20e7-5b9c-bfdf-57f701ad6150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11y-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436561} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba8cfa2f-c627-57d0-923a-8380a85a57e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436601}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f88992c6-7672-5688-a790-113b251f1d96" :question/math-academy-id "q-159721" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{6x+11y}{\\sqrt{y}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{6x+11y}{\\sqrt{y}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6x+11y)\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-(6x+11y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y})}{{(\\sqrt{y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(11\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-(6x+11y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{22y-(6x+11y)}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\right)}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{11y-6x}{2y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=11y-6x.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0163c90f-63f7-520c-b90b-cdca85bc5861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566364} {:answer/id #uuid "78d2aa47-e366-536d-979b-7aaddb43183d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566591} {:answer/id #uuid "90f591ac-d503-53e4-9edf-df0ecead1c36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566647} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8aa054-536b-5175-8e3d-21f8ecd92148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566710} {:answer/id #uuid "c62a4f9c-30eb-5f65-9868-b6c9578e4d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6y-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78d2aa47-e366-536d-979b-7aaddb43183d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566591} :answer-field/id #uuid "5af82be6-e454-517f-89c6-df6d183337b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566918}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1691ed28-0c5c-54a8-9012-9dfc00861f65" :question/math-academy-id "q-159719" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{3y-2x}{7y-6x}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{(7y-6x)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{3y-2x}{7y-6x}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3y-2x)\\cdot (7y-6x)-(3y-2x)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(7y-6x)}{(7y-6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (7y-6x)-(3y-2x)\\cdot (-6)}{(7y-6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14y+12x+18y-12x}{(7y-6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4y}{(7y-6x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=4y.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60243795-2a92-591c-983d-ab0a12df51fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}^{2}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566544} {:answer/id #uuid "7ccef17a-7e81-5ad2-b543-a2a7ee459876" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-y)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566601} {:answer/id #uuid "b662e7db-0fcb-5572-a49f-f705511b1c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}^{2}⁡(x-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566724} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f81ca3-bfba-5c9f-b61e-29a424ecf9f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}^{2}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566781} {:answer/id #uuid "e65931e8-e876-5d62-8009-c6a3aab5a425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}^{2}⁡(x-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60243795-2a92-591c-983d-ab0a12df51fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}^{2}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566544} :answer-field/id #uuid "a55eaa90-3c66-5bf4-a7e7-2ac1f5a2db6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566958}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d644ebc-b214-5b17-9daa-3ced5a3257b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-159712" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)}{{e}^{x+y}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{{e}^{x+y}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)}{{e}^{x+y}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y))\\cdot {e}^{x+y}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x+y})}{{({e}^{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}^{2}⁡(x-y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-y)\\cdot {e}^{x+y}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)\\cdot {e}^{x+y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)}{{({e}^{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}^{2}⁡(x-y)\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{x+y}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)\\cdot {e}^{x+y}\\cdot 1}{{({e}^{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}^{2}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)){e}^{x+y}}{{({e}^{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}^{2}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y)}{{e}^{x+y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=\\operatorname{sec}^{2}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-y).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2621e07c-5376-55e5-8cbe-302266f28c89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698760} {:answer/id #uuid "2e29c9d0-d84b-5149-901e-003ad0823432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698762} {:answer/id #uuid "9e3ff607-b55e-51f4-9e23-51a1b0e12aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698773} {:answer/id #uuid "caae950d-8ead-5c06-b75c-9caeb8e64350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698775} {:answer/id #uuid "f561e67f-b76c-5d17-93fb-eb5b44189b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e29c9d0-d84b-5149-901e-003ad0823432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698762} :answer-field/id #uuid "30058bce-34f1-536c-b32f-4adde94f543f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698764}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "908d866d-c5d2-5fac-9d5d-89bc64f4361a" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x^2-y^2}{e^{y-x}}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(1,0)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant. In particular, the chain rule gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}e^{y-x}=-e^{y-x}.\n$$\n\nApply the quotient rule before evaluating at the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\n&=\\frac{2x e^{y-x}-(x^2-y^2)(-e^{y-x})}{(e^{y-x})^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{2x+x^2-y^2}{e^{y-x}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow substitute $x=1$ and $y=0$:\n\n$$\n\\left.\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\right|_{(1,0)}\n=\\frac{2+1-0}{e^{-1}}=3e.\n$$\n\nThe denominator is always positive, so the function and this derivative are defined at the given point."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "238115dd-b58b-5e08-94d5-b7da915bda70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y e^{xy^2}\\bigl((x+y^2)-1\\bigr)}{(x+y^2)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698759} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcec15b-23b1-5788-becc-ee1d0c36a87c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y e^{xy^2}\\bigl(x(x+y^2)+1\\bigr)}{(x+y^2)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698761} {:answer/id #uuid "2ef07d99-eb44-5adb-850e-20c77cf3ad3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y e^{xy^2}\\bigl(x(x+y^2)-1\\bigr)}{x+y^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698763} {:answer/id #uuid "5a3c65db-f38e-5e5f-a132-ad0dfce469b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{xy^2}\\bigl(y^2(x+y^2)-1\\bigr)}{(x+y^2)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698765} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6ee467-6f19-54ee-9b74-e70055683cd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y e^{xy^2}\\bigl(x(x+y^2)-1\\bigr)}{(x+y^2)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f6ee467-6f19-54ee-9b74-e70055683cd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y e^{xy^2}\\bigl(x(x+y^2)-1\\bigr)}{(x+y^2)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698769} :answer-field/id #uuid "9920d21b-94b2-53d3-9ac4-48f700e9964b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698772}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9537a10a-ace7-5581-a0a1-2a2907755cd0" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{e^{xy^2}}{x+y^2},\n$$\n\nfind $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$, where $x+y^2\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant. The numerator contains a composite function, so use the chain rule to differentiate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}e^{xy^2}\n&=e^{xy^2}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(xy^2)=2xy e^{xy^2}, \\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(x+y^2)&=2y.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth numerator and denominator depend on $y$. Apply the quotient rule, preserving the subtraction and the squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\n&=\\frac{(2xy e^{xy^2})(x+y^2)-e^{xy^2}(2y)}{(x+y^2)^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{2y e^{xy^2}\\bigl(x(x+y^2)-1\\bigr)}{(x+y^2)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $2y e^{xy^2}$ is common to the numerator terms; it cannot be canceled with the sum $x+y^2$ in the denominator. The derivative is defined wherever $x+y^2\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f3d54d-ab52-50bb-9399-11584f498a06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x-12y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698757} {:answer/id #uuid "1b082d39-9ba2-5cc7-bffc-0f946a61987a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698758} {:answer/id #uuid "71bdaab4-8266-50e2-9b5c-b716cd1fac86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698766} {:answer/id #uuid "7572906f-f58e-533c-8832-a74b080fe0fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698767} {:answer/id #uuid "862708d0-5d80-5d64-bcf2-b3ab61244dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-6y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b082d39-9ba2-5cc7-bffc-0f946a61987a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698758} :answer-field/id #uuid "e565c205-0d11-58fe-a260-964a57426bc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698776}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "acb99466-30f7-53aa-bbea-e3163ae8199e" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2x+3y}{x-2y}$. The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{(x-2y)^2}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant. The numerator and denominator derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(2x+3y)=3,\n\\qquad\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(x-2y)=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\n&=\\frac{3(x-2y)-(2x+3y)(-2)}{(x-2y)^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3x-6y+4x+6y}{(x-2y)^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{7x}{(x-2y)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing with the supplied form gives $h(x,y)=7x$. These formulas apply where $x-2y\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c8fd8c5-6636-5e91-9b5d-b9c3574b9eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699051} {:answer/id #uuid "70a877e2-1ec4-5764-8712-d8c81c1773f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699061} {:answer/id #uuid "8b5cbe67-a840-5e5d-9107-1de6c255be97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699064} {:answer/id #uuid "97d99df0-33ec-592a-ad8a-2352e9c17ad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699066} {:answer/id #uuid "cb02d79a-4e33-5f0c-ace6-141265e770e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c8fd8c5-6636-5e91-9b5d-b9c3574b9eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699051} :answer-field/id #uuid "50f6b31d-0957-53d2-9aa8-cd2406c30d29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699055}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30e79f3c-ebf9-5ee3-a9f7-87af4f4fcb8e" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{- 2 x^{2} - 3 y^{2} - 2}{\\sqrt{y}},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(-1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Write $N=- 2 x^{2} - 3 y^{2} - 2$ and $D=\\sqrt{y}$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{y}&=- 6 y, \\\\\nD_{y}&=\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the square root use $D_{y}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}$.  Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{N_{y}D-ND_{y}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(- 6 y\\right)D-N\\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{2 x^{2} - 9 y^{2} + 2}{2\\left(y\\right)\\sqrt{y}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step multiplies the numerator and denominator by $2\\sqrt{y}$ and collects the numerator terms. Now substitute the point, after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\right|_{(-1,1)}&=\\frac{\\left(-6\\right)\\left(1\\right)-\\left(-7\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}{\\left(1\\right)^2} \\\\\n&=- \\frac{5}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n These expressions apply where $y>0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699053 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f1b6cbd-f7d9-5fe2-972b-64df4cf135e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699059} {:answer/id #uuid "7038eabb-d3b2-5911-99b6-4e82904ad863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 10 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699060} {:answer/id #uuid "8988e03f-7dc7-5c83-bea0-20efe459bcfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699063} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c5a81b-f88b-54b2-bc75-0a2d97cb3d23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699073} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b7f256-c429-54eb-9dda-0171a068c312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f1b6cbd-f7d9-5fe2-972b-64df4cf135e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699059} :answer-field/id #uuid "99d7b05b-efdd-5a2b-b0ff-b4998030c128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699067}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3a50981f-7ca4-5e15-8f03-ccedc12a95e1" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{3 x^{2} + y^{2} - 1}{e^{x - y}},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(-1,2)$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Write $N=3 x^{2} + y^{2} - 1$ and $D=e^{x - y}$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{y}&=2 y, \\\\\nD_{y}&=- e^{x - y}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule differentiates the exponent first; its inner derivative is $-1$. Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{N_{y}D-ND_{y}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(2 y\\right)D-N\\left(- e^{x - y}\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3 x^{2} + y^{2} + 2 y - 1}{e^{x - y}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step factors the common nonzero exponential $e^{x - y}$ from the numerator. Cancel that factor with one copy in the squared denominator. Now substitute the point, after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\right|_{(-1,2)}&=\\frac{\\left(4\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{e^{3}}\\right)-\\left(6\\right)\\left(- \\frac{1}{e^{3}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{e^{3}}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&=10 e^{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n These expressions apply where $e^{x - y}\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "298e3d07-1f2d-5109-b0cc-77fc0d81ba76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699050} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb008dc-1883-536b-8f24-4d08d1cb7c4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699054} {:answer/id #uuid "c44c4920-c231-5fc4-91ec-58bd3d67ae50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699074} {:answer/id #uuid "ce19b885-267c-5aab-aaec-93f040f3bab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699076} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d9bcb3-819d-56a1-89d8-a7bd7c97b00e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce19b885-267c-5aab-aaec-93f040f3bab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699076} :answer-field/id #uuid "b73b08c7-e4ce-5809-a128-3e614c54420b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699071}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65fd193d-d9ad-588d-b4ba-ecfbf36bcbb7" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{- 2 x y - 3}{2 x - 2 y - 1},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(0,-1)$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $y$ constant and differentiate with respect to $x$. Write $N=- 2 x y - 3$ and $D=2 x - 2 y - 1$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{x}&=- 2 y, \\\\\nD_{x}&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{N_{x}D-ND_{x}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(- 2 y\\right)D-N\\left(2\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{4 y^{2} + 2 y + 6}{\\left(2 x - 2 y - 1\\right)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step distributes the subtraction and collects like terms. Now substitute the point, after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\right|_{(0,-1)}&=\\frac{\\left(2\\right)\\left(1\\right)-\\left(-3\\right)\\left(2\\right)}{\\left(1\\right)^2} \\\\\n&=8.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n These expressions apply where $2 x - 2 y - 1\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6054e7e8-2357-5453-bd28-df85d4eb8c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{11}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699057} {:answer/id #uuid "78f4bb71-0114-5502-a1db-84bdceafc211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699062} {:answer/id #uuid "a870b043-9b68-5135-a982-62e2ad93ba52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699068} {:answer/id #uuid "b239eabb-7538-52a4-9db9-a9f0228631fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699070} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4c368d-35fd-5a0e-84da-c4ee8a0adf06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b239eabb-7538-52a4-9db9-a9f0228631fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699070} :answer-field/id #uuid "f614a711-2ef1-5129-aeee-a489173aa3c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699082}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b7ce85a3-231b-52d3-9284-683bab4a239d" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{- 3 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}}{e^{- x + y}},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(-1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $y$ constant and differentiate with respect to $x$. Write $N=- 3 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ and $D=e^{- x + y}$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{x}&=- 6 x, \\\\\nD_{x}&=- e^{- x + y}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule differentiates the exponent first; its inner derivative is $-1$. Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{N_{x}D-ND_{x}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(- 6 x\\right)D-N\\left(- e^{- x + y}\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{- 3 x^{2} - 6 x - 2 y^{2}}{e^{- x + y}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step factors the common nonzero exponential $e^{- x + y}$ from the numerator. Cancel that factor with one copy in the squared denominator. Now substitute the point, after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\right|_{(-1,1)}&=\\frac{\\left(6\\right)\\left(e^{2}\\right)-\\left(-5\\right)\\left(- e^{2}\\right)}{\\left(e^{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{e^{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n These expressions apply where $e^{- x + y}\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069a3cc8-1f1a-58da-86e1-87122723c5f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699049} {:answer/id #uuid "5bbcd7f4-5d73-5025-8d63-f1900f36e341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699056} {:answer/id #uuid "b17e4500-ffa5-52a8-ae36-d19f109ceb0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699069} {:answer/id #uuid "f2769889-c75a-55fa-bfac-791733aba4ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699080} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b72858-5e76-56ca-8872-41a50fa6584a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "069a3cc8-1f1a-58da-86e1-87122723c5f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699049} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c0e2180-1398-56bb-b1e3-b5f23c0dce37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699065}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f39f470f-1381-5c00-9d56-dd5568a45b1b" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{x y - 3}{- x + 2 y},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(-1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Write $N=x y - 3$ and $D=- x + 2 y$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{y}&=x, \\\\\nD_{y}&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{N_{y}D-ND_{y}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(x\\right)D-N\\left(2\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{6 - x^{2}}{\\left(- x + 2 y\\right)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step distributes the subtraction and collects like terms. Now substitute the point, after differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\right|_{(-1,1)}&=\\frac{\\left(-1\\right)\\left(3\\right)-\\left(-4\\right)\\left(2\\right)}{\\left(3\\right)^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{9}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n These expressions apply where $- x + 2 y\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703527 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec93c9c-71c3-5ae4-83cb-91b5486e7a3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(x - y^{2} + 2 y + 2\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703520} {:answer/id #uuid "17859394-c3b9-5fc6-86ee-30d777b553f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 4 x y + 4 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703522} {:answer/id #uuid "63aefc19-d9d6-572d-90b5-b6c3bb5a273a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 4 x y + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703525} {:answer/id #uuid "64f9b0a6-0bd6-5de1-b34c-49b252145591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{3} y + 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 8 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{5} + 8 x y^{3} - 6 x y - 2 y^{3} + 4 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703526} {:answer/id #uuid "74a79ef0-3666-518c-9796-b95b2dc621fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 4 x y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63aefc19-d9d6-572d-90b5-b6c3bb5a273a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 4 x y + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703525} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb699f6d-64e6-5b05-97e1-9befcde14bd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703539}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "71a49800-4e41-562a-b2c1-6a13ec64df46" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}}{x - y^{2} + 2},\n$$\n\nfind $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$, where $x - y^{2} + 2\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Write $N=e^{- x y^{2}}$ and $D=x - y^{2} + 2$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{y}&=- 2 x y e^{- x y^{2}}, \\\\\nD_{y}&=- 2 y.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule differentiates the exponent first; its inner derivative is $- 2 x y$. Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{N_{y}D-ND_{y}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(- 2 x y e^{- x y^{2}}\\right)D-N\\left(- 2 y\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 4 x y + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 2\\right)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step factors the common nonzero exponential $e^{- x y^{2}}$ from the numerator.  These expressions apply where $x - y^{2} + 2\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eef394c-6c6e-53fa-903a-281cf2754aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(2 x y^{2} + 2 y^{4} - 4 y^{2} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2} - 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703521} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d5adf2-a8e1-5126-93b1-233dbb5b7fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} - 2 y^{2} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2} - 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703538} {:answer/id #uuid "ca60e663-b106-5aef-b768-ee7310651bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} - 2 y^{2}\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2} - 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703541} {:answer/id #uuid "df78e23f-a774-5a65-8e8d-b6362bef4112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(-1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2} - 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703544} {:answer/id #uuid "fbce868f-eb8d-554d-8345-c5b610dd04d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{4} + y^{6} - 2 y^{4} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2} - 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9d5adf2-a8e1-5126-93b1-233dbb5b7fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} - 2 y^{2} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2} - 2\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703538} :answer-field/id #uuid "87803f06-3701-5ac9-ae0f-c8724c9eec66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703531}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95022efe-9e94-52c7-acd3-6f1bc4536d2a" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}}{x + y^{2} - 2},\n$$\n\nfind $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$, where $x + y^{2} - 2\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $y$ constant and differentiate with respect to $x$. Write $N=e^{x y^{2}}$ and $D=x + y^{2} - 2$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{x}&=y^{2} e^{x y^{2}}, \\\\\nD_{x}&=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule differentiates the exponent first; its inner derivative is $y^{2}$. Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{N_{x}D-ND_{x}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(y^{2} e^{x y^{2}}\\right)D-N\\left(1\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} - 2 y^{2} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2} - 2\\right)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step factors the common nonzero exponential $e^{x y^{2}}$ from the numerator.  These expressions apply where $x + y^{2} - 2\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703542 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d768e01-2289-5785-99ff-806ad1db0a9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703523} {:answer/id #uuid "7228ef8b-0a13-5afa-98ec-44ee79efb8be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} - 2\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703528} {:answer/id #uuid "879e6303-660d-57a2-8c0e-89e646bb43e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4}\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703532} {:answer/id #uuid "9a59dca4-32b0-5131-82f7-46bab1079e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x + y^{2} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703536} {:answer/id #uuid "acb662e1-a992-574b-b262-fec6c874374e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} + 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d768e01-2289-5785-99ff-806ad1db0a9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703523} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c36b5e4-f056-5adf-9d3f-cc5234f01eca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703530}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d55c8998-0b4c-5e3d-89d2-d34076862d70" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}}{x + y^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$, where $x + y^{2}\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $y$ constant and differentiate with respect to $x$. Write $N=e^{x y^{2}}$ and $D=x + y^{2}$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{x}&=y^{2} e^{x y^{2}}, \\\\\nD_{x}&=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule differentiates the exponent first; its inner derivative is $y^{2}$. Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{N_{x}D-ND_{x}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(y^{2} e^{x y^{2}}\\right)D-N\\left(1\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{e^{x y^{2}}\\left(x y^{2} + y^{4} - 1\\right)}{\\left(x + y^{2}\\right)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step factors the common nonzero exponential $e^{x y^{2}}$ from the numerator.  These expressions apply where $x + y^{2}\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d41f55d-ea6e-54c3-8ad4-cb6a40022e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{3} y + 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 4 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{5} + 4 x y^{3} - 2 y^{3} + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 1\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703519} {:answer/id #uuid "3838472f-384c-5a74-9830-5a9502829a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 4 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{3} - 4 x y + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 1\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703524} {:answer/id #uuid "94349017-cc0b-523c-bb23-17e5b2e68ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 2 x y + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 1\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703533} {:answer/id #uuid "950e8626-bcd5-5ffc-9c19-eb9df7b478ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 2 x y + 2\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 1\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703535} {:answer/id #uuid "e126372e-913a-54ce-974e-39a5a0328279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 2 x y + 4 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 1\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94349017-cc0b-523c-bb23-17e5b2e68ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 2 x y + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 1\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703533} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd8e9b5-cb29-52a9-a70a-d795c78950e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703540}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d602471f-8233-53fe-90e9-d195b0f0e982" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}}{x - y^{2} + 1},\n$$\n\nfind $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$, where $x - y^{2} + 1\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Write $N=e^{- x y^{2}}$ and $D=x - y^{2} + 1$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{y}&=- 2 x y e^{- x y^{2}}, \\\\\nD_{y}&=- 2 y.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule differentiates the exponent first; its inner derivative is $- 2 x y$. Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{N_{y}D-ND_{y}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(- 2 x y e^{- x y^{2}}\\right)D-N\\left(- 2 y\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 2 x y + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 1\\right)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step factors the common nonzero exponential $e^{- x y^{2}}$ from the numerator.  These expressions apply where $x - y^{2} + 1\\ne0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "453d9798-d79d-5357-b594-39c83563a78c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703586} {:answer/id #uuid "4e21f254-b085-56ba-b52d-0510163f8767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{3} y + 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x y^{5} + 2 x y - 2 y^{3}\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703587} {:answer/id #uuid "b8741453-4ca9-579e-adb2-a32b6cc2a070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703595} {:answer/id #uuid "ba1686a8-0609-5876-9d71-8ec3a13cd105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} + 2\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703596} {:answer/id #uuid "f74f925c-53a5-517a-b377-74d00c5bf435" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ